Find the area of this triangle, correct to one decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (4,0);
\coordinate (R) at (-1.2,2.07846);
\draw (P)--(Q)--(R)--cycle;
\path (P)--(Q) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\path (P)--(R) node[midway,left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\pic[draw=black,"$120^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.55cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=Q--P--R};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

This triangle has an area of $42\text{ cm}^{2}$. Find $x$, correct to two decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3.6,0);
\coordinate (R) at (3.63731,2.1);
\draw (P)--(Q)--(R)--cycle;
\path (P)--(Q) node[midway,below] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (P)--(R) node[midway,above left] {$x\text{ cm}$};
\pic[draw=black,"$30^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.8cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=Q--P--R};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A quadrilateral garden $ABCD$ is divided by diagonal $AC$ into two triangles. The diagram shows its side lengths and included angles. Find the total area, correct to one decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (6.5,2.59808);
\coordinate (D) at (1.5,2.59808);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (A)--(C);
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$} (B) node[below right] {$B$} (C) node[above right] {$C$} (D) node[above left] {$D$};
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ m}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$6\text{ m}$};
\path (C)--(D) node[midway,above] {$10\text{ m}$};
\path (D)--(A) node[midway,left] {$6\text{ m}$};
\pic[draw=black,"$120^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.45cm,angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=C--B--A};
\pic[draw=black,"$120^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.45cm,angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=A--D--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
